.TH NETWATCH-NG 1 "November 2026" "NETWATCH NG 2.x" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
netwatch-ng \- Linux network supervision and administration TUI
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B netwatch-ng
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B netwatch-ng
starts the NETWATCH NG terminal user interface for Linux network
discovery, device identification, gateway inspection, Wi-Fi inventory,
and management of NETWATCH-owned firewall and traffic rules.
.PP
The interface is keyboard-driven and can be used in a local terminal or
over SSH. It does not start a graphical desktop application.
.SH PRIVILEGES
Read-only inspection should normally be performed as an unprivileged user.
Operations that change firewall or traffic-control state require root
privileges. Start the application from a privileged terminal only when
those operations are needed.
.SH OPTIONAL TOOLS
NETWATCH NG detects optional system tools at runtime. Depending on the
feature, these may include nmap, iw, rfkill, iptables, nft, tcpdump,
aircrack-ng, avahi-browse, snmpwalk, ethtool, mtr, and iperf3.
Missing optional tools are reported by the application.
.SH TRAFFIC LIMITS
The current traffic manager uses tc clsact packet policing. Packets
exceeding the selected rate are dropped. This is not smooth queue-based
HTB shaping. NETWATCH NG does not replace an interface's root qdisc.
.SH SAFETY
Firewall and traffic-control operations are limited to resources that
NETWATCH NG can identify as its own. Do not use network-control features
on systems or networks without authorization.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/netwatch-ng/
System configuration directory.
.TP
.I /var/lib/netwatch-ng/traffic-state.json
Protected state used to identify NETWATCH-owned traffic filters.
.TP
.I ~/.config/netwatch-ng/
Per-user configuration directory for unprivileged operations.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ip (8),
.BR tc (8),
.BR nmap (1)
.SH AUTHOR
NETWATCH NG maintainers
